// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
// Filename:	 Bus Pirate  VSC90 Translight PCB.test
// Project:		VSC90
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    24/05/24
//
// Description: using the Bus Pirate & Probe kit to test the PCB
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.

#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box below.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
//DISPLAY: lamptrayPCB1.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#2: Equipment Setup 1
a. Using TE159 connect the PSU to the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Connect the PC (via USB) to K5 on the Test box (TE209).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable PSU.
d. Connect the PC to the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
//DISPLAY: TE132.jpg
CLICK_OK:


#3: Equipment Setup 2
a. Connect the UUT to the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Connect the VSC90 Translight Spot PCB TE213 to the UUT(Refer to setup picture below).
b. Place the UUT inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
c. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
DISPLAY: TE213.png
CLICK_OK:
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3: 

#4: Configure the PSU
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1

#4.1: Power on the test box.
Press the I/O Power button on the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209) to turn on.
DELAY: 9000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.111 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
IF:
GOTO: #4.2: 
IMPORTANT: This test has failed, check the power button has been pressed, power supply, USB connection and the ftdi chip.		
PASS_FAIL: #4.1
GOTO: #5

#4.2: Connect to the test box
CONNECT: VSC90
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4.1:


#4: WHITE 5000K LEDs test:
a. Check that ONLY the WHITE 5000K LEDs (LED11, LED12, LED13, LED14) are ON.
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSFLOOD 0010 1023
DELAY: 2500
// PASS_FAIL: #4:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.825 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSOFF


#5: IR 850/860NM LEDs test:
a. Check that ONLY the IR 850/860NM LEDs (LED21, LED22, LED23, LED24) are ON.
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSFLOOD 0001 750
DELAY: 2500
// PASS_FAIL: #5:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.621 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSOFF

#6: UV 365NM LEDs tests.
a. Check that ONLY the  the UV 365NM LEDs (LED31, LED32, LED33, LED34) are ON.
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSFLOOD 1000 1023
DELAY: 2500
// PASS_FAIL: #6:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.820 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSOFF

#7: Turn off any LEDs still on
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSOFF


#8: Spot WHITE 5000K  test:
a. Check that ONLY the WHITE SPOT LED (LED1) is ON.
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSSPOT 0001 1023
DELAY: 2500
// PASS_FAIL: #8:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.372 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSOFF


#9: Spot IR  850nm test:
a. Check that ONLY the IR LED 850nm LED (LED2) is ON.
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSSPOT 0010 750
DELAY: 2500
// PASS_FAIL: #9:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.296 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSOFF


#10: IR LED 780nm LED test:
a. Check that ONLY the IR LED 780nm LED (LED3)is ON.
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSSPOT 1000 1023
DELAY: 2500
// PASS_FAIL: #10:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.299 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
COMMAND: VSC90 TRANSOFF




#11: Test complete
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:

#Failed: A test failed
a. This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
b. Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: Test's Complete
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish.
DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
DISCONNECT: VSC90
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
// End of file
